<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Awdaghast</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Awdaghast was a trading town in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>, that served as a terminus of trans-Saharan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a>. It was linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-trade">gold trade</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> captured it in 1054, weakening Ghana's hold on the trade.</p></div>
